.TH "SKOGAI RUNNER-JOURNAL" 1  "skogai runner-journal 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai runner\-journal \- session journals (runner.journal in .skogai): read them back, harvest them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai runner journal\fR <COMMAND>
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skogai runner\-journal\-prompts(1)
only the user's input, one json row per turn
.TP
skogai runner\-journal\-harvest(1)
agents pick decisions, docs, todos and learnings out of a journal

the journal is cut into chunks of \-\-turns turns, each chunk goes to one
worker with schema `harvest`. stdout is one json array of every item.
